Q: How to pass a std::thread::scope as a parameter with another reference A: <p><code>std::thread::Scope</code> looks like this:</p>
<pre class="lang-rust prettyprint-override"><code>pub struct Scope&lt;'scope, 'env: 'scope&gt; { ... }
</code></pre>
<p>If you apply the same pattern to your function, it works:</p>
<pre class="lang-rust prettyprint-override"><code>fn test2b&lt;'scope, 'env: 'scope&gt;(
    scope: &amp;'scope std::thread::Scope&lt;'scope, 'env&gt;, 
    data: &amp;'env String
) {
    scope.spawn(move || {
        println!(&quot;print out {}&quot;, data);
    });
}
</code></pre>
<p><a href="https://play.rust-lang.org/?version=stable&amp;mode=debug&amp;edition=2024&amp;gist=c56f834277789a8681dc0cc39e06c3ac" rel="nofollow noreferrer">playground</a></p>
